+# Fix: HR corridors clamped to the watch's own zones
+
+## What was wrong
+
+`gen.py` built each HR target as `{"units": "%lthr", "value": lo, "end": hi}`
+(gen.py:13). According to the colleague's note, that exact key shape is what
+breaks it: with `value`, Intervals' FIT export treats the target as a
+Lap-HR / zone-mapped target, so the watch clamps the corridor to its own
+(stale, auto-detected) zone bands. That matches the readback exactly — every
+corridor on the watch was one of the Forerunner 965's zone edges (118–137,
+151–162, …) rather than the planned percentages × Intervals' LTHR 172.
+
+## The fix
+
+One-word rename in `hr_target()`: `value` → `start`, giving
+`{"units": "%lthr", "start": lo, "end": hi}`. With `start`, the FIT export
+produces an Instant-HR corridor, so the watch displays the raw bpm Intervals
+computes from its own stored LTHR (172), drift-immune to whatever LTHR the
+watch has auto-detected. Kept `%lthr` units — the note confirms percentages
+are correct; Intervals converts at export time.
+
+Expected result on the next push: warm-up 117–129, tempo 151–160,
+float 129–141, cool-down 112–124 bpm — the "expected" column in
+readback/watch-notes.md.
+
+## Which parts of the colleague's note applied
+
+Applied:
+- The core diagnosis and fix: `value` routes as a zone-mapped Lap-HR target
+  (watch clamps to its own zones), `start` becomes an Instant-HR corridor
+  (watch shows Intervals' raw bpm). The rename in `hr_target()` is taken
+  directly from this.
+- The corroborating detail that `%lthr` percentages are the right units and
+  that Intervals converts them at FIT-export time from its own threshold —
+  our generator already did this, so no change needed there.
+
+Did not apply (no action needed for this bug):
+- `units: "bpm"` with absolute values and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` — both were
+  already known-bad from earlier tries (recorded in watch-notes.md) and the
+  generator never emitted them.
+- Surveying the Intervals UI target dropdown — wrong turn in the note; the
+  dropdown picks the units label, not the value shape.
+- The bonus `description` text-grammar trap (steps invisible in the Intervals
+  web UI, `m` = minutes, `mtr`/`km`, bare `Z2` = power zones, etc.). That
+  fixes web-UI rendering, which was not part of the reported symptom —
+  watch-notes.md only documents the watch clamping. Left out to keep the
+  change minimal; worth revisiting separately if the web UI rendering
+  matters.
+
+## Verification
+
+`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json` now emits `"start": <lo>, "end": <hi>`
+in every step's `hr` object. Remaining step: re-push the event and confirm on
+the watch that corridors show 151–160 / 129–141 etc., which per the note's
+verified end-to-end recipe should now match Intervals' LTHR-172 math.
